<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abbeville</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abbeville is a town in the Somme <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somme-river">River Somme</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was the capital of the County of Ponthieu and a prosperous cloth town, with the Gothic church of Saint-Vulfran. Prehistoric stone tools found nearby by Jacques Boucher de Perthes in the 19th century gave their name to the Abbevillian culture.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abbeville.jpg" alt="Abbeville" width="320" height="486" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Emmanuelhammel · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mus%C3%A9e_Boucher-de-Perthes.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
